  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Find the gravitational force of attraction between the ring and sphere as shown in the diagram, where the plane of the ring is perpendicular to the line joining the centres. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt><mi>R</mi></math> is the distance between the centres of a ring (of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>) and a sphere (mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>) where both have equal radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0120_7b0497660c8d.png\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 133px;\" /></p>"
